# scripts/check_static.py runs this (ported from geistlib #342). Left out, each
# for a reason:
#  - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: lengths before the arrays they
#    describe put adjacent size_t on purpose; style, not a bug.
#  - DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling: asks for C11 Annex K, which no toolchain
#    here ships; it flags every fprintf and memcpy.
#  - optin.performance.Padding: field order follows meaning, not size.
Checks: >-
  -*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding
HeaderFilterRegex: '(src|include|tools)/.*'
